Subject: fix(forge): parse enterprise raw content URLs

ParseRawContentURL accepts only raw.githubusercontent.com. A harness that
sources a skill or script from the forge it is running on therefore fails to
load with `not a raw.githubusercontent.com URL: <host>`, even though the URL is
one this CLI built for that forge.

An enterprise install has no raw.githubusercontent.com. It serves the same
bytes from the appliance, with a literal "raw" segment after the repository
instead of a separate hostname:

  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{owner}/{repo}/{ref}/{path...}
  https://{host}/{owner}/{repo}/raw/{ref}/{path...}

Accept the second when the host is the one GITHUB_SERVER_URL names, which is
the same variable the rest of the CLI uses to decide where the forge is. The
"raw" segment is required rather than optional: without it the ref would be
read from the wrong position and the parse would succeed while pointing at a
path that does not exist.

Carry the host through as the forge name, too. A directory source is fetched
over git rather than HTTP, and CloneURL turns the forge name back into a host,
where "github" means github.com. Labelling an enterprise URL "github" sends
that fetch to the public site, which fails with "not our ref" against a commit
that only exists on the appliance.

The public host keeps its behaviour, its forge name, and its original error
message, which callers match on.

Breadboard note: patches Go source, so it belongs to the build patch list in
deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh, and it applies on top of patches 0005
and 0006. Written to be sent upstream as-is. Add a DCO sign-off before
submitting it as a human-authored change.

--- a/internal/forge/url.go
+++ b/internal/forge/url.go
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
